==Russian==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Slavic|jьmę|lang=ru}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|h₁nḗh₃mn̥|lang=ru}}. The so-called '''[[н]]'''-declension of this and nine other similar neuter nouns stems from the fact that the word-final '''-[[я]]''' was the nasal vowel [[Ѧ]], [[ѧ]] (little [[yus]]) in [[Old Church Slavonic]] and Late Proto-Slavic, resulting in the '''-ен-''' before all the case endings in the modern language. Compare the declension of Old Church Slavonic {{term|sc=Cyrl|имѧ|tr=imę|lang=cu}}.

